details.image_prompt:
[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene is composed as a 3/4 overhead shot at a 40-degree angle, capturing two rustic matte ceramic bowls placed on an aged oak wooden surface with visible grain and natural use marks. The main bowl is in sharp focus, while the second bowl sits slightly behind and to the side, softly blurred. Each bowl contains a generous, rustic portion of the Mediterranean chicken and chickpea stew; the chicken thighs, cut into irregular, bite-sized pieces, are visible alongside tender, softened half-moon zucchini slices and plump chickpeas coated in a vibrant, textured crushed tomato sauce. The dish features a rich, deep red color from the tomatoes, contrasted by the golden-brown edges of the sautéed chicken and the deep purple of the halved kalamata olives. A few vibrant green specks of dried oregano are scattered throughout. Propped casually beside the primary bowl is a rumpled, off-white linen napkin and two halves of warm, slightly charred whole-wheat pita bread. Lighting is soft and natural, originating from a window on the left, casting gentle, subtle shadows and creating a slight sheen on the tomato sauce. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating — lived-in, warm, authentic. Not a sterile studio setup. Slight natural imperfections: an asymmetric garnish placement, a small sauce drip on the bowl rim, slightly uneven browning on the chicken. Include subtle traces of the cooking process: a few rogue chickpeas and a small pita crumb on the wooden surface. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature — cozy and inviting, not cold or clinical. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. The image should be indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a printed cookbook."
]
